& [RuntimeIdentity] is deterministic shared semantic state governance
  + [SAIR-001] independent inference jobs coordinate through canonical machine-readable frames and typed events
  + [SAIR-002] the runtime does not share or alter model hidden state KV caches token generation or provider processes
  + [SAIR-003] agreement seals a coordination checkpoint and does not prove external truth

& [ParticipantContract] is role-bound
  + [SAIR-004] every participant has stable identity and at least one FacultyKind
  + [SAIR-005] every mutation author and attestor must be declared in the frame participant map
  + [SAIR-006] settlement requires exact-digest acknowledgement from every required participant
  + [SAIR-007] acknowledged coverage must include Observer Honesty and Security even when one participant carries more than one role

& [CanonicalFrame] is immutable-by-transition
  + [SAIR-008] frame identity includes profile generation predecessor digest purpose policy participants propositions constraints anchors evidence challenges focus capacity applied delta references status semantic digest and frame digest
  + [SAIR-009] semantic digest covers meaning-bearing frame content while frame digest additionally covers generation lifecycle and accounting metadata
  + [SAIR-010] all machine collections are deterministically ordered and unknown serialized fields are refused
  + [SAIR-011] proposition epistemic status is observed inferred assumed imagined or verified and its evidence source and dream lineage remain explicit

& [DeltaReconciliation] is one atomic successor
  + [SAIR-012] every batch member names the exact base generation frame digest policy and known author
  + [SAIR-013] the runtime verifies each delta digest sorts deltas by identity rejects duplicate identities and rejects multiple mutations of one target
  + [SAIR-014] all references and operation preconditions validate against the staged successor before commit
  + [SAIR-015] any fault refuses the complete batch and returns no changed frame
  + [SAIR-016] successful nonempty reconciliation increments generation exactly once records all delta identities and emits deterministic transition identity and digest
  + [SAIR-017] imagined propositions are refused in ordinary reality-frame deltas

& [StreamingCapacity] applies deterministic backpressure
  + [SAIR-018] capacity regions are pinned anchors current focus retrieved associations recent stream and reserved headroom and their checked sum cannot exceed context budget
  + [SAIR-019] P0 measures batch novelty in canonical serialized UTF-8 bytes and labels this as a proxy rather than model-token usage
  + [SAIR-020] novelty greater than reserved headroom returns BUFFERED with required and available amounts and leaves the base frame byte-identical
  + [SAIR-021] recovery actions preserve the event log and instruct freeze classify cluster prioritize split compact reconcile and resume
  + [SAIR-021C] COMPACT binds one exact base and one declared Refiner then may retain a subset of current focus and monotonically reduce focus retrieval and recent-stream proxy accounts while preserving propositions constraints anchors and evidence
  + [SAIR-021D] compaction requires evidence records its own lineage recomputes headroom without changing the context budget or pinned-anchor account and produces one ordinary working successor

& [Settlement] is a two-phase same-digest gate
  + [SAIR-022] PREPARE changes WORKING to CANDIDATE_FROZEN only when challenges are empty and recomputes identity
  + [SAIR-023] every attestation binds participant faculty candidate digest disposition rationale evidence and attestation digest
  + [SAIR-024] missing acknowledgement yields INCOMPLETE dissent yields REVISION_REQUIRED and defer yields DEFERRED
  + [SAIR-025] only complete exact-digest role coverage changes the candidate to SEALED and emits a receipt over both candidate and sealed digests
  + [SAIR-026] no semantic proposition is reclassified by settlement

& [DreamFrame] is bounded hypothetical state
  + [SAIR-027] FORK requires one SEALED parent frame exact parent digest purpose preserved invariants relaxed assumptions forbidden effects hypotheses consequences evidence requirements falsification conditions and bounded branch depth
  + [SAIR-028] hypotheses are IMAGINED and the branch cannot authorize or perform effects
  + [SAIR-029] dream status is OPEN TESTING VERIFIED or DISCARDED and transitions are closed
  + [SAIR-030] VERIFIED requires declared evidence requirements satisfied and exact-digest Observer Honesty and Security acknowledgement
  + [SAIR-031] promotion from VERIFIED produces an ordinary ASSUMED or INFERRED delta against the same sealed parent generation and digest
  + [SAIR-032] promotion never mutates the parent and must pass normal reconciliation and settlement before entering later reality

& [PureP0Boundary] is deliberately narrow
  + [SAIR-033] implementation belongs in cantor_core as pure Rust with no IO clock randomness unsafe code network provider effect or persistence
  + [SAIR-034] it reuses SemanticId ContentDigest FacultyKind and cryptographic canonical serialization already present in core
  + [SAIR-035] ProcedureCoordination remains unchanged because it schedules instructions while this runtime governs shared semantic frames
  + [SAIR-036] JSON round trip deterministic replay positive negative and non-mutation tests are required
  + [SAIR-037] optional CLI transport proof may follow only after core acceptance and may not imply distributed deployment

& [Acceptance] is measurable
  + [SAIR-A01] preserved source manifest canonical signature and seven-fold trace verify
  + [SAIR-A02] deterministic batch reconciliation accepts nonconflicting deltas and byte-identically replays
  + [SAIR-A03] stale base invalid digest unknown participant conflicting target bad reference and imagined reality mutation each refuse atomically
  + [SAIR-A04] capacity overflow buffers with exact accounting and no frame mutation then valid Refiner compaction can reclaim headroom and permit a later exact-base reconciliation
  + [SAIR-A05] freeze and settlement require empty challenges exact participant coverage exact digest and Observer Honesty Security gates
  + [SAIR-A06] dissent defer and incomplete attestation cannot seal
  + [SAIR-A07] DreamFrame cannot fork from unsealed state cannot escape effects or epistemic label and cannot promote before verified review
  + [SAIR-A08] verified promotion returns a typed non-authoritative delta and leaves its sealed parent unchanged
  + [SAIR-A09] workspace formatting tests warnings-denied lint and regression pass

& [AuthorityBoundary] is pure reversible P0 implementation authority
  + permits forms validation deterministic transitions receipts tests fixtures machine-form round trips and local effectless experiment output
  + excludes network transport llama.cpp modification model calls signing keys distributed consensus persistent service autonomous effects FPGA deployment and claims of truth intelligence consciousness or P equals NP

